Sora and JetBrains Mono (self-hosted web fonts)
==========================================================

Used by every page under docs/ (the landing pages, the docs, the roadmap
and the blog) for --font-display/--font-body (Sora) and --font-mono
(JetBrains Mono). Self-hosted so the pages load no font from an external
CDN.

Source
------

Every file is byte-identical (`cmp`) to the file of the same weight and
style in these packages; the sha512 is the npm registry's dist.integrity:

  @fontsource/sora@5.3.0
    https://registry.npmjs.org/@fontsource/sora/-/sora-5.3.0.tgz
    sha512-SqW3OpKxxfKvxDLPlbdrWf2KooPfbd+W3jaYn483o+Y/JrmU87vjFPNptDqwP428c3vY+gnranLhjcbRaXB0Jw==

  @fontsource/jetbrains-mono@5.3.0
    https://registry.npmjs.org/@fontsource/jetbrains-mono/-/jetbrains-mono-5.3.0.tgz
    sha512-fqDfB5I9f1p1TV486aUgB9t8zP84P0O1FtQR5Ol9vjwPy+S+EIGlVYm1cvj2W5shcZMTg2nZFdVMoH5wFu8a1A==

Files
-----

  sora-latin-{300,400,500,600,700}-normal.woff2
  JetBrainsMono-Regular.woff2  (weight 400 normal)
  JetBrainsMono-Bold.woff2     (weight 700 normal)
  JetBrainsMono-Medium.woff2   (weight 500 normal)
  JetBrainsMono-Italic.woff2   (weight 400 italic)

Latin subset only, no `unicode-range`: every use of JetBrains Mono is plain
ASCII (case numbers, PINs, timestamps, code, the wordmark), and a narrow
range without a second face would only lose coverage.

Sora has no italic face upstream, so no page asks for italic Sora; emphasis
uses weight or colour instead. `test_every_docs_page_font_usage_has_a_matching_font_face`
checks that every (family, weight, style) a docs page uses has a shipped
`@font-face`, with no exceptions.

The application
---------------

`app/static/fonts/` is not in the repository: the Dockerfile copies the six
faces `app/static/css/fonts.css` declares (Sora 400/500/600/700, JetBrains
Mono Regular/Bold) from this directory into the image. One copy serves both
the site and the app.

License
-------

SIL Open Font License 1.1 for both families: `sora-LICENSE`,
`jetbrains-mono-LICENSE`, unmodified as shipped by their packages.

Variable fonts of the website (docs/_fonts, never copied to the site)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

openwhistle.net ships one variable file per family instead of the static cuts above (those stay
for the app image and the diagram code). The originals are committed unchanged; scripts/build_site.py
cuts them to the weights the CSS uses and to the drawn text, and inlines the result into
assets/css/fonts.css (fonts-italic.css for the italic). SIL Open Font License 1.1: sora-LICENSE,
jetbrains-mono-LICENSE.

  Sora[wght].ttf                    wght 100-800 (site: 300-700)
    https://github.com/sora-xor/sora-font/blob/7f9a9c5d0ccd1c099cfac420aa27133df1c5fdc4/fonts/variable/Sora%5Bwght%5D.ttf
    commit 7f9a9c5d0ccd1c099cfac420aa27133df1c5fdc4
    sha256 84ff7096ae3ec6c8be47d906d1a0ba4de7f2ce78c615275c77301964a316e16c

  JetBrainsMono[wght].ttf           wght 100-800 (site: 400-700)
  JetBrainsMono-Italic[wght].ttf    wght 100-800 (site: 400, one instance)
    https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono/releases/download/v2.304/JetBrainsMono-2.304.zip
    release v2.304, fonts/variable/ in the zip (sha256 of the zip
    6f6376c6ed2960ea8a963cd7387ec9d76e3f629125bc33d1fdcd7eb7012f7bbf)
    JetBrainsMono[wght].ttf         sha256 662a196d58f1183bf2d77428b6d5283fe3f45161ab021bea4036bc98e5cac016
    JetBrainsMono-Italic[wght].ttf  sha256 f115aaa12113718c02ce72864fe6823b87241bc23d3e44cf1220155f861063f2

OpenType features kept: fontTools' default set (kern, liga, calt, ccmp, locl, mark, mkmk, ...) and
tnum. Dropped, because no stylesheet asks for them: aalt, case, dlig, salt, ordn, sinf, subs, sups,
zero, ss01, ss02, ss19, ss20, cv01-cv99. The italic mono is cut to the text pages draw in it.
